{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Implementation + landing log for 4144-2784-6437-4efb (tireless-ruinable-prairiedog).\n\nVERIFICATION OF THE PLAN'S FACTUAL CLAIMS (all re-checked against the tree, not taken on trust):\n- `correctness` / `edge-cases` are named in the base reviewer's evidence contract\n  (src/rebar/llm/reviewers/code-review-base.md) and are NOT in OVERLAY_IDS. Confirmed.\n- DEFAULT_BLOCK_THRESHOLD = 0.95 in llm/code_review/registry.py; neither id had a routing\n  entry, so both resolved through it. Confirmed.\n- The 8.0% operator-accepted friction budget is recorded on the `tests` entry's _comment\n  (\"blocks 99 changes / 8.0%, operator-accepted\"). Confirmed.\n- THE MEASUREMENT REPRODUCES EXACTLY. Re-ran the new --block-impact mode over the local\n  .tickets-tracker corpus: 1262 changes; correctness 715 surviving / 62 would-block / 51\n  changes / 4.04% / mean validity 1.00 / 0 below 0.5; edge-cases 485 / 27 / 22 / 1.74% /\n  0.99 / 0; concurrency 1 / 0 / 0 / 0.00%. Byte-identical to the table now committed.\n- The \"corrections to the originating claim\" also reproduce: c3aec3eae6's code-v3 sidecar\n  carries its correctness finding at priority 0.3857 / validity 0.7143 (below 0.54), and\n  d2dea317ec has no code-v3 sidecar at all.\n\nTWO CLAIMS IN THE DRAFTED DOCUMENT WERE WRONG AND WERE CORRECTED BEFORE PUSH:\n- \"every would-block finding was verifier-confirmed at validity >= 0.99\" is FALSE. The\n  MEANS are 1.00 and 0.99, but the lowest single would-block finding is 0.9286 for both\n  criteria. Restated as mean-plus-minimum.\n- \"neither exceeds a twentieth of the friction budget\" is FALSE. 4.04% of an 8.0% budget is\n  half of it, and 1.74% is under a quarter. Restated with the real fractions